WEBVTT

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.970
Alright! We won! It's a huge upset!

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.860
Dash forth, my hound.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.950
Go, Tsubaki!

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.920
We have enough men back to defend! Don't be rash!

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:35.630
Zaki!

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.640
Akasaki! You're in a good spot!

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.640
Damn you, Tsubaki. Who do you think you are to make me run?!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.650
You've already wasted two definite goals.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:58.820
I'll make fun of your afro from now on if you miss that!

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.620
Alright!

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.250
Natsuki!

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.930
I can't answer it right now! Someone get it please!

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.100
Wow, three consecutive wins, eh?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.940
Yeah! We're on a roll!

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.560
I'm glad.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.070
Hi, this is East Tokyo United's PR department,

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.160
where I'm the sole worker.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.450
N-Nagata?

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:47.990
What?

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:52.500
Seriously?!

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.000
For the national team?!

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.340
So this time around,

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:02.010
Akasaki has been called up to the team that'll represent Japan in the Olympics.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.930
He will miss the next league match,

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.970
but he'll be working hard as ETU's representative.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.730
I hope you guys will send him off with that in mind.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.650
Yeah, our representative!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:17.730
Congratulations, Akasaki!

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:20.740
Amazing!

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.990
Our team is sending out a national player?!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.780
I only played with him yesterday,

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.620
but for some reason, he's emitting this incredible aura now!

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.670
This is surprising, right, Sera?

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.720
What's wrong with you?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.510
I want to get a call-up, too!

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.640
If I hadn't sat out the last two matches,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.480
I might have unleashed my potential and got noticed!

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.560
There's nothing you could do about it.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.400
Your shoulder was injured after all.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:02.570
Oh yeah, Sera's also in the age bracket that's eligible to play in the Olympics.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.280
That applies to you as well, Tsubaki.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:04.900
Huh?

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.580
We're too old to be called up...

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.910
I'm kind of jealous.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:15.000
You're going to be famous among the girls now, Zaki.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.670
Are you implying that I wasn't popular to begin with?

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.460
Alright, Akasaki, get ready.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.550
Sure.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.420
Manager, do you have anything to say?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.770
Congratulations, Akasaki.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:41.820
You're the first national player to emerge in my managing career.

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.070
I couldn't be happier for you.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.990
Make the most of this opportunity.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:51.870
T-Thanks...

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.580
Well then,

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:57.620
Those of you who have had lil' playing time, rejoice!

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.590
This is your chance! Akasaki's starting spot is vacant!

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.960
Of course, if you play better than Akasaki,

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.090
you might even become a regular.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.720
W-What the hell?!

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.970
Why are you saying that now?

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.930
Well, isn't it true?

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.190
Even if it's just one match, you will be playing for another team.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.110
We'll be moving forward during that time.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.730
If you don't learn anything while you're there,

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.610
you might not have a place to come back to.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.120
Fine, fine, I got it.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.620
Hah! Serves you right, Akasaki!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.000
You're gonna get swept off your feet if you're not careful!

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.000
Kuro, you're suspended for the next game since you got carded again, right?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.000
You better watch your feet, too.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.210
Alright, go get 'em!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.300
Yes!

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.340
Good luck, Akasaki!

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.760
Go get cocky!

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.470
Be as flashy as you want!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.310
Is that your idea of cheering me on?!

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:02.900
Alright, we should get started, too.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.820
It's been two years since I became the general manager.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:12.410
We've experienced many failures, but we were finally able to get some results.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:16.240
There are many clubs who don't like sending players to the national team,

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.580
but for a small club like us,

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.750
this is the best chance for us make ourselves known.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.670
Hey there, run! Use your heads!
It's all thanks to you, Tatsumi.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.340
Hey there, run! Use your heads!

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:31.010
Your way of doing things has yielded results.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.640
Kamei! They're going for the back!

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:47.070
Watch out!

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.230
I won't let you!

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.150
Yeah!

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.950
Nice, Murakoshi!

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.990
Nice cover, Koshi!

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.580
I'm sorry, Koshi.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.000
I've been making the same mistakes.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.130
You're letting the pressure get to you!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.670
You can handle that fine if you just do the usual drill.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:14.180
Geez, what is he doing?

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:21.930
Man, Chiba's manager is making life hard for us.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.520
Right after the game started,

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.310
he noticed that Sugie and Kamei don't fit that well together.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:31.190
Ever since then, he's been attacking Kamei's position.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:34.780
It's not that Kamei's lacking in match fitness,

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:38.280
he just took a little longer to get into the game.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.160
However, they latched onto that.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:46.250
They must've been planning for that when they knew Kuro's not playing.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.460
Miyano's in the same situation.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.880
Since they're resticting Gino,

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.220
he's been isolated on his side.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:56.680
Shall we switch them out?

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:57.600
No, we won't.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:03.060
They need to have a taste of the action so that they'll be motivated to work harder.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:12.230
You might have stood a chance with your best lineup,

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:16.740
but league matches aren't that easy.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:19.280
Hey! Push the line higher up!

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:23.750
You're going to experience this even more in the future.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.130
Well, we didn't lose.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:39.140
I guess we'll just be taking one point home, eh?

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:45.810
Man, he's not listening to me at all...

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.650
H-He did it!

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.900
Akasaki did it!

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:55.400
The Olympic under-23 teams of Japan and Hong Kong faced off.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.910
Even though Japan dominated possession in the first half,

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:02.330
neither of the three shots at the goal were successful.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:05.960
Kubota of Osaka Gunners hit the cross bar,

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.080
and the first half ended 0-0.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.380
25 minutes into the second half,

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.710
Akasaki, who was subbed in,

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:15.050
tried his luck from this position.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.510
See, it's Akasaki!

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:24.310
And Ootani of Shimizu Impulse slotted it in to hand Japan the lead!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.810
After painfully defending this lead,

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:28.890
Japan is one step closer to the Olympics.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.690
Akasaki played an active role!

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.860
That shot would have gone in without any help!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.490
Damn you Ootani, for getting in the way!

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.570
Y-Yuri...

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:44.870
Argh, if that had been Akasaki's goal,

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:48.460
our club would have received much more attention!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.710
Let's not talk about that right now.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.800
He's thinking about something again.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:02.390
I hope he's not up to something crazy again.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.660
Yeah!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.240
Another victory against Yokohama!

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:29.330
With this, we've qualified for the next round of the Japan Cup!

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:32.000
Yay!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.130
It's been three years since we made it to the top eight!

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.500
The cup is next!

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:38.260
Yuri, I think that's a bit premature.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.550
Good game, Motoki.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:51.140
Damn it! It's really frustrating to lose to this guy!

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:57.400
Nice goal, Prince!

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.740
Thanks, Seri.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.410
Now we're past the Japan Cup preliminaries!

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:06.620
Oh, today was a cup match?

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.750
I totally didn't keep track of that.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.410
Hey, Gino!

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:14.080
Did you have a bad day or something?

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.420
You didn't send me as many passes as usual!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:20.880
No, I supplied you the usual amount,

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:26.390
but it's true that my performance today is nothing to rave about.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:29.890
That goal should have gone in without the keeper touching it.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:33.980
To be honest, my left leg is a bit swollen.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.360
Maybe I should sit out the next match.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.730
Tatsumi!

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:44.320
It looks like my leg's tired.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:47.490
Can I sit out the next match?

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:49.790
W-What are you saying?!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.500
How are we supposed to go up against Kawasaki without you?!

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.380
Okay, I'll think about it.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.340
Hey! Manager!

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.510
Geez, a match without Prince...

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:15.480
Well, even though the swelling of his leg isn't anything serious,

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.520
it's probably true that he's worn out.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:21.570
It's the same case for everyone.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.860
We're halfway into the season,

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:26.030
so there's bound to be fatigue.

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.830
Still, Prince is playing through the matches at a high tempo.

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:34.580
That's true.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:41.130
Last year, he even got tired of a match and requested to be subbed out.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:46.630
Crazy things did happen, didn't they...

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:48.930
They are still happening now, though.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:55.180
However, Prince is playing so well this season that nobody's complaining.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:58.770
It must have suited him really well...

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.980
Tatsumi's playing style, that is.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.440
Yeah.

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:09.950
Still, I wonder how Tatsumi plans on facing Kawasumi without Prince.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.410
Hmm...

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.340
Yup, let's go with that.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.350
Gotou!

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.020
Oh, what's up, Tatsumi?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:40.600
You know... I'm so hungry.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.610
And, uh?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:47.820
Will you treat me to curry? An extra big serving while you're at it?

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:49.740
Curry?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:53.120
Hey, guys.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.370
Hi.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.870
Do you like curry?

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:58.620
Curry?

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:02.130
Yup, curry. Don't like it?

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:05.920
Well, I guess I like it.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.630
But what are you talking about?

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:10.180
Then, please go ahead and buy these.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:12.140
Here's the money and the list of ingredients.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:16.640
I had the cafeteria ladies write that, so it should be correct.

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:20.020
Uhh...

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.900
It's chicken curry.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:25.650
Chicken is better for athletes, right?

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:29.400
I thought about going for Victory-Cutlet-Curry so we can win against our opponents,

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.950
but that's too cheesy.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:32.910
Alright.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.240
Don't get the amount wrong.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.910
Get going now.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:42.880
W-What about practice?

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:50.550
The hell is this?

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:54.300
What do you mean? It's a leaflet.

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.510
That's not what I meant!

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:02.810
Why do we have to hand these out in town instead of practicing?!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.150
I didn't sign up for this.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:08.320
Besides, what the hell is a curry party?!

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:13.070
I mean, don't most people like curry?

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.490
That's not the point!

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.080
Can't you be serious for a minute?!

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:21.410
Anyway, I am sick and tired of your random games!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:24.330
Do it alone if you wanna play them!

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:32.840
I can't believe that a pro player is refusing to interact with the local fans.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.350
Those are two different matters altogether!

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:42.100
Oh, I get it! People won't come if it's Kuro.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:44.350
Sugie, can you do this instead?

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.860
Only 15 minutes, okay?!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.370
Oh, really? I'll leave it up to you then.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:00.040
Let's go, Sugie, Tsubaki!

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:07.250
Hey, don't you think you're going a bit too far with your games?

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:12.260
Ha! Don't think you don't have work to do, Murakoshi.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:17.800
Hey! We're going to make curry for 100 people,

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.760
so those who are free, help out!

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.520
Stop dwaddling! You're free, right?!

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:24.310
Tatsumi!
Stop dwaddling! You're free, right?!

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.980
Why are you doing this without informing the PR department?!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.770
Wow, you look good in that.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:33.740
He even enlisted the help of the formidable cafeteria ladies.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.280
Just what is he planning?!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.780
Wait, are you planning to get all of us involved?

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.790
Yup, everyone's gonna make curry together.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.810
Hope you'll be tasty.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:11.900
We're having a curry party at ETU's clubhouse!

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.320
It's free of charge!

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.820
ETU's on a winning streak!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.580
Would you like to eat curry?

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.670
It's Tsubaki!

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.380
Tsubaki is here!

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:32.960
Hey!

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.090
Please sign for us!

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:37.090
What are you doing here?!

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:40.840
What's this? A curry party?

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:42.180
It's today!

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:43.350
For real?!

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:47.270
Yeah, I'm not sure myself,

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.560
but everyone's involved.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.400
Will all the players be there?

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.860
Uh, yeah.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.110
We're going!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:18.340
Oh, he's so handsome!

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:19.130
Ciao.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:48.160
Hey, I was out for a while, and what's all the commotion about, Tatsumi?

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:53.170
Gotou, we're just having a curry feast.

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:58.170
There must be other ways to let the players relax.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:01.840
What if something bad happens?

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.220
Nothing will happen.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:10.180
Look, everyone is eating the curry peacefully.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:12.270
The curry is really good!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:13.190
The players,

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:14.230
Get in line.

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:16.190
the management,
Get in line.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.150
Akasaki, how was playing in the national team?

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.690
the local people,

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:24.490
the cafeteria ladies, and the junior coaches.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:27.450
They're all here, sharing this moment together.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.290
Good luck, young man.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:35.540
Thanks.

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:38.210
This is what a club is, Gotou.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:43.720
There are only 11 people playing on the field.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:47.470
But you can't get through the long season with just that.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:51.680
Those on the bench, the management, the fans...

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.100
There are many people connected to the club.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:21:00.570
All of them have to be united and fight for the same cause.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:07.240
ETU will become much more stronger if that happens.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:10.790
You're right.

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:26.470
Make way!

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:29.010
The king has returned!

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:37.020
Certainly, we saw it there -

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:42.440
A dream-like reality where a weak team defeats a strong one.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.780
We saw the miracle known as Giant Killing.

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:02.800
Tatsumi...

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:07.590
Can ETU do it?

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:13.220
Yeah, these guys can do it.

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:15.600
They can become such a club.

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:18.190
I see...

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:23.320
So, please take care of these bills.

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:26.110
Wait, it's coming out of my pocket?!

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:29.820
You said you'd treat me, didn't you?!

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:57.020
The season is far from over!

00:22:57.770 --> 00:22:59.390
Let's go take them on!

00:22:59.390 --> 00:23:00.850
Yeah!
